      {
        "id": 224887,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-01-03T23:18:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Ulf316\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/u/edb3f5/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ulf316:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>No, they don’t. In fact, they can and did easily leave a false impression. Other priorities have been assumed by people in my area as:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Aeon KS</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Void Guard</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>One Deck Dungeon</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Not full Oblivaeon implementation. By providing the info that it won’t happen until after ALL the above AND now Oblivaeon digital, it changes the narrative. So no, the information was NOT out there in any substantive way. It is now.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>All they say is that it will done in a future update with no timeline or impression given beyond that. &nbsp;Handelabra if you follow them doesn’t give out release dates for updates until they are ready. &nbsp; Once it’s ready I’m sure Handelabra will make it well known.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:58:22.598Z",
