      {
        "id": 224888,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-01-03T23:20:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Ulf316\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/u/edb3f5/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ulf316:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>so I will cease using this forum for this line of discourse \"</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I guess I’m forced to be more blunt, then: Good luck with that. Since I suspect that most other venues for this line of discourse will be even more tilted towards wanting digital OA first out of the two.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Ulf316\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/u/edb3f5/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ulf316:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My only contributions after that admission is to specifically refute what I consider to be gloss</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>They’ve consistently before now said nothing more specific than “OA will be available in Sidekick will be available in a future update” and as someone who keeps tabs on Handelabra I can note that when it comes to Sentinels they’ve been very clearly&nbsp;putting a strong focus on getting digital OA finished and that it’s something a lot of people have been asking after, while conversely there’s not been much mention at all of Sidekick other than the similar “it’s still on our to-do list and it will be done when it’s done” sentiments.</p>\n<p>So you have my sympathies that you made an assumption about the missing information that turned out to be incorrect and so ended up with some dashed hopes, but that doesn’t refute things or show a change in the narrative, it just means you made an incorrect assumption.</p>\n<p>Edit: Also will second Sonvar’s statement that Handelabra has a policy across the board of never giving solid release dates until something is very definitely ready for release so you’d be highly unlikely to get a firm ETA right now&nbsp;regardless.</p>",
